<ontology/use_calico_printing/use_calico_printing__doc_bichromate_of_potash__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 48" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n48> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Bichromate of Potash used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 48"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "BICHROMATE OF POTASH: a beautiful crystalline salt in large prisms, of a brilliant red color, used in dyeing and calico printing, obtained from chromate of iron, and which is the source of the chrome pigments. Mixed with sulphuric acid, it is a powerful oxidizing agent for bleaching oils and fats."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
